From a9b4d9845962a1e30450502e3d2bd45a5e34b6a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 13:30:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: SMART_EVENT_RESPAWN fired twice on spawn (I-338)

Upstream #25482 set TriggerJustRespawned in the Creature constructor so that
non-compat spawns get JustRespawned. SmartAI::InitializeAI already fired
SMART_EVENT_RESPAWN for a live creature, so every DB-spawned SmartAI creature ran
its respawn actions twice: once from InitializeAI during AddToWorld, once from
Creature::Update on the first tick.

Idempotent actions hide it; anything that spawns state does not. Goblin Captive
38643 casts 72243 (summon Oomlot Shaman 38644) on respawn, so quest 24925 'Free
the Captives' shipped two shamans stacked on each other per captive. Stock content
is affected too (Scarlet Miner mine cars, Artruis, Jormuttar).

Fire the event from InitializeAI only for temp summons, which skip the
JustRespawned path per #25533; everything else now gets it exactly once.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/server/game/AI/SmartScripts/SmartAI.cpp | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/server/game/AI/SmartScripts/SmartAI.cpp b/src/server/game/AI/SmartScripts/SmartAI.cpp
index 7c6c24e02..244b30f93 100644
--- a/src/server/game/AI/SmartScripts/SmartAI.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/AI/SmartScripts/SmartAI.cpp
@@ -1047,7 +1047,15 @@ void SmartAI::InitializeAI()
     {
         mJustReset = true;
         JustReachedHome();
-        GetScript()->ProcessEventsFor(SMART_EVENT_RESPAWN);
+
+        // Every freshly created creature now has TriggerJustRespawned set (#25482), so
+        // Creature::Update delivers JustRespawned - and with it SMART_EVENT_RESPAWN - on its
+        // first tick. Firing the event here as well would run every respawn action twice, which
+        // is invisible for idempotent actions (flags, morphs, auras) but duplicates anything
+        // that spawns state: a summon on respawn produces two creatures stacked on each other.
+        // Temp summons skip the JustRespawned path (#25533), so they still need the event here.
+        if (me->IsSummon())
+            GetScript()->ProcessEventsFor(SMART_EVENT_RESPAWN);
     }
 }
 
